
# <type>(<optional scope>): <subject>
#
# <body: what changed and why, wrapped at 72 characters>
#
# <footer: BREAKING CHANGE: <description>, Refs #<issue>>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits - https://www.conventionalcommits.org
#
# The type drives the automatic release (python-semantic-release):
#   feat      a new feature                               -> minor
#   fix       a bug fix                                   -> patch
#   perf      a performance improvement                   -> patch
#   build     packaging, build system, dependencies       -> no release
#   ci        CI configuration                            -> no release
#   docs      documentation only                          -> no release
#   refactor  code change that neither fixes nor adds     -> no release
#   style     formatting, no code change                  -> no release
#   test      adding or fixing tests                      -> no release
#   chore     anything else (tooling, maintenance)        -> no release
#
# Breaking change -> major: add "!" after the type/scope (feat!: ...)
# or a "BREAKING CHANGE: ..." footer.
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lower case, no final period, <= 50 chars.
#   e.g. fix(crism): use the right directory for FRT0001xxxx IDs
#
# Lines starting with "#" are ignored.
